  "question": {
    "text": "If one were to apply the Bohr model to a particle of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>'</mo></math>&nbsp;and charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>'</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>'</mo></math> moving in a plane under the influence of a magnetic field &#39;B&#39;, the energy of the charged particle in the <math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> level will be:",
